<article class="env-lemma" id="0DTA">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DTA">Lemma <span data-tag="0DTA">78.11.6</span>.</a> Let $B \to S$ be as in Section <a href="/tag/043A" data-tag="043A">78.3</a>. Let $(U, R, s, t, c)$ be a groupoid in algebraic spaces over $B$. Let $B' \to B$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces. Then the base changes $U' = B' \times _ B U$, $R' = B' \times _ B R$ endowed with the base changes $s'$, $t'$, $c'$ of the morphisms $s, t, c$ form a groupoid in algebraic spaces $(U', R', s', t', c')$ over $B'$ and the projections determine a morphism $(U', R', s', t', c') \to (U, R, s, t, c)$ of groupoids in algebraic spaces over $B$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. Hint: $R' \times _{s', U', t'} R' = B' \times _ B (R \times _{s, U, t} R)$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>